      "id": 238119,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-06-03T15:40:36.517Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don’t have a problem with it, personally, but it does rub me the wrong way when the person plays that hero in a way that is completely different from the actual hero. (Imagine Legacy actually dropping a car on a normal person – that kind of thing. And yes, things like that have happened.) It’s their character, so I won’t tell them what they can or can’t do, but it’s grating… <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/unamused.png?v=9\" title=\":unamused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":unamused:\"></p>\n<p>Luckily the justification of “this isn’t the canon universe” is a great excuse to wave away my concerns. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-06-03T15:40:36.517Z",
      "reply_count": 1,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
